Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
for BDD frame work test
--------------------------------
Run smoke tests:
behave --tags=@smoke
As per the tags we need to give that marker name
Run all tests:
behave
-------------------------------------
for pytest
To run all tests in suite:
pytest
To log the data:
pytest -v -s
target specific browser:
pytest --browser firefox --browser webkit
for tag before run that we need to mark @pytest.mark.smoke on function:
pytest -m smoke  ---> -m for mark
to skip the test @pytest.mark.skip
Stop executing immediately upon the very first test failure:
pytest -x
to run specific test:
pytest Tests/test_login.py
to run specific function:
pytest Tests/test_login.py:test_log
trace automatically on failure:
pytest --tracing retain-on-failure
parallel execution:
pytest -n 4
capture screenshot:
pytest --screenshot=only-on-failure
generate allure report:
pytest --alluredir=reports/allure-results
show report:
allure serve reports/allure-results


-----------------------------------------
Assumptions
OrangeHRM demo site is stable and accessible at https://opensource-demo.orangehrmlive.com/.

Demo credentials (Admin/admin123) remain valid.

Demo data resets periodically, so created users may not persist across sessions.

Tests are executed locally in a Python virtual environment.
-------------------------------------------
Limitations
Current implementation validates workflows only via UI automation; no API checks are included.

Demo environment may occasionally be slow or reset, leading to flaky results.

No parallel execution configured yet, so regression runs may take longer.

Reporting is limited to Behave’s console output.

---------------------
Suggested Improvements
Reporting: Integrate Allure or HTML reports for better visibility.

CI/CD: Run Behave tests in GitHub Actions or Azure DevOps pipelines for continuous validation.
-------------------------------------
QA/Automation Approach Summary
Maintainability: Adopted Page Object Model (POM) for reusable, clean, and modular code.

BDD-style clarity: Feature files describe workflows in business-readable language, improving collaboration.

Classification strategy: Tagged scenarios as @smoke (critical path) and @regression (broader coverage).

Modern QA mindset: Focused on reporting, CI/CD integration, and hybrid strategies to improve release confidence.

Engineering decisions: Chose Playwright for fast, reliable browser automation and Behave for structured BDD.